To verify the property specification, a third external property assertion code was created and is included here:

```C#
[Combinatorial]
[TestMethod]
public void TestMethod1(
    [PexUseRepresentation(typeof(ArrayList)), PexAssumeValid]
    ArrayList arrList,
    [PexUseRepresentation(typeof(int)), PexAssumeValid]
    int x)
{
    // arrList.Add(x);
    int oldCount = arrList.Count;
    bool containsBeforeAdd = arrList.Contains(x);
    arrList.Add(x);
    bool containsAfterAdd = arrList.Contains(x);
    Assert.IsTrue(containsAfterAdd == true && containsBeforeAdd == false 
        && arrList.Count == oldCount + 1);
}
```

### Conclusion

In conclusion, these automatic testing tools are becoming essential for automated testing, validation of model-based properties, coverage measurements, and regression tests. However, it is also important to remember that blackbox testing tools are not a substitute for property-based testing. Different requirements and use cases should still be thoroughly covered with traditional black box testing as well. Manual validation of test cases and outputs can also provide unparalleled quality control.

